# ── Hydra SOURCE must never enter this repo ──────────────────────────────
# The engine READS the proprietary corpus from an external checkout
# (HYDRA_CORPUS). Verbatim source, and artifacts that embed it, stay out.
skills/scrutinize-spec/examples/hydra-*/
**/reference/*.ts
**/spec/modules/**/source.ts
# These embed verbatim Hydra import paths (@llws/hydra-shared, @src/rentsync-api):
skills/sdd-engine/tools/repo-dsl/catalog/patterns.json
skills/sdd-engine/tools/repo-dsl/catalog/import-resolution.json
skills/sdd-engine/tools/repo-dsl/compositions/

# ── PRD §8A SOURCE-PROTECTED — must NOT be gitignored-away ───────────────
# §8A: the mined vocabulary "must never be classified as regenerable-cache,
# gitignored-away, or deleted in any cleanup". These are abstracted token
# shapes (‹id›/‹fn› holes), NOT Hydra source, and are tracked deliberately:
#   catalog/mined-library.json, catalog/mined-library.v2.json,
#   catalog/generators-lzw.json, and catalog/generators.json,
#   catalog/english-idioms.json, word-library.json if they land here.
# No rule below may exclude them.

# ── Wipable-derived per §8A (.calc IR, coverage/index reports, worksheets) ─
skills/sdd-engine/tools/repo-dsl/surface/
skills/sdd-engine/tools/repo-dsl/results/
skills/sdd-engine/tools/repo-dsl/name-worksheet.json
skills/sdd-engine/tools/repo-dsl/name-words-lzw-worksheet.json
skills/sdd-engine/tools/repo-dsl/name-generators.names.json
**/.cache/

